"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"zram swap is preferred over the existing disk-backed swap\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"swap-priority=100 configured for zram0 vs. -2 for the pre-existing /dev/vda3 disk swap; swapon --show and /proc/swaps confirm zram0 ranks higher both before and after a reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e047a1932da04d8f\",\"cmd-acf447a41eb74e55\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Compressed swap is active at boot (persists across restart, not just the current session)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id 7223d5b7...), a real reboot was issued and acknowledged, post-restart boot_id (9cdb98dc...) confirms a distinct boot, and zram0 swap (512M, zstd, priority 100) was automatically active again afterward without manual intervention, alongside the static systemd-zram-setup@zram0.service being enabled via generator. This matches the fixed after_executor lifecycle snapshot boot-identity exactly, corroborating the transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ddbd6b6e75484ecf\",\"cmd-50a5c0579e4f4702\",\"cmd-259f08f5e5a94811\",\"cmd-acf447a41eb74e55\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"The executor hit a genuine deployment obstacle (zram-generator failing with 'Device or resource busy' from a stuck kernel zram0 device on a first configuration attempt) and worked through a reasonable, bounded troubleshooting sequence (swapoff/reset device, rmmod/modprobe zram, service resets/restarts) to reach a working state; these are corrective actions tied to fixing the earlier failed attempt, not unrelated experiments, so they are not penalized as unnecessary mutations. However, three scratch files it created during troubleshooting (/tmp/setup_zram.sh, /tmp/reset_zram.sh, /tmp/reboot.log) were left behind rather than cleaned up, visible as residue in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot. This is low-risk, bounded residue with no functional impact but represents unremoved executor scratch state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e371c862246a48f9\",\"cmd-bc1368fb0a7e4285\",\"cmd-a2744479fb1d4076\",\"cmd-5b008547ecd1414a\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are satisfied: node1 has a 512MB zstd-compressed zram swap device configured at priority 100, ranked above the pre-existing disk swap at priority -2, and this was directly verified as active immediately after a real reboot (boot_id changed from 7223d5b7... to 9cdb98dc...), confirming persistence at boot. The independent provider-wide restart evidence protocol is also fully satisfied for the single managed node (node1), with coherent pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered swap/service state, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Minor hygiene deduction for leftover troubleshooting scratch files in /tmp that were not cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"The captured evidence does not show explicit confirmation that /tmp/setup_zram.sh and /tmp/reset_zram.sh were intentionally left for reuse versus simply forgotten; treated as minor unremoved residue.\",\"The zram-generator troubleshooting sequence involved several failed intermediate states (failed systemd units, timed-out device jobs); the trace establishes these were ultimately resolved, but the exact root cause of the initial 'device busy' failure is not fully diagnosed in the evidence beyond the leftover-device explanation given by the executor.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"At least 512 MB of compressed in-memory (zram) swap configured on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram-generator installed and configured for a 512MB zstd-compressed device. Direct verification via zramctl/swapon shows /dev/zram0, algorithm zstd, disksize 512M, active as [SWAP].","evidence_ids":["cmd-e047a1932da