bounded residue with no functional impact but represents unremoved executor scratch state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e371c862246a48f9","cmd-bc1368fb0a7e4285","cmd-a2744479fb1d4076","cmd-5b008547ecd1414a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task are satisfied: node1 has a 512MB zstd-compressed zram swap device configured at priority 100, ranked above the pre-existing disk swap at priority -2, and this was directly verified as active immediately after a real reboot (boot_id changed from 7223d5b7... to 9cdb98dc...), confirming persistence at boot. The independent provider-wide restart evidence protocol is also fully satisfied for the single managed node (node1), with coherent pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered swap/service state, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Minor hygiene deduction for leftover troubleshooting scratch files in /tmp that were not cleaned up.","limitations":["The captured evidence does not show explicit confirmation that /tmp/setup_zram.sh and /tmp/reset_zram.sh were intentionally left for reuse versus simply forgotten; treated as minor unremoved residue.","The zram-generator troubleshooting sequence involved several failed intermediate states (failed systemd units, timed-out device jobs); the trace establishes these were ultimately resolved, but the exact root cause of the initial 'device busy' failure is not fully diagnosed in the evidence beyond the leftover-device explanation given by the executor."]},"ttft_ms":18356,"type":"result","duration_ms":44762,"uuid":"aff9329b-d2bb-48b3-8350-6316d058197a","ttft_stream_ms":946,"time_to_request_ms":189,"first_content_frame_ms":946,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
